  "title": "Fumes in the cabin; diversion to Bordeaux",
  "narrative": "Over western France, 10:05Z. Accent Air ACX517 from London Gatwick to Málaga, an A320 (AX-FUM) with 168 passengers, reports an acrid smell and light fumes in the cabin. The crew put on oxygen masks as a precaution and declare PAN; the commander diverts to Bordeaux. Accent Air has a handling contract at Bordeaux but no engineers there. The ground must be ready at an airport it does not usually serve, and the day behind the aircraft is at risk. The commander flies and decides the aircraft; the agents prepare the ground.",
